out.push(note('Row 6 is the one to mark, and it is a good illustration of how a register degrades. "At both ends of a hire" is a day in the sense that matters — it is a trigger — but it was in the owner column of the learner\'s table at stage 4 and fell out when the row was written up. A reviewer who copies the line and says so has done band 4; one who adds that the correction costs the writer the neat column widths of a table they have already laid out has done the Book 2 move. The three-way count adding up is the other thing to check, and it should be checked arithmetically every time, because a count that does not add up means a row was classified twice or not at all.'));
out.push(stage('6R', 'Share'));
out.push(p('⚠ **Add the three numbers out loud against the number of acts.** ⚠ **It takes ten seconds and it catches the one fault that makes a register useless** — **a row counted in two groups, or in none, which means the author does not know the state of their own obligations.**'));
out.push(stage('7', 'Write freely – sample (233 words)'));
